{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/353213-unexpected-divine-superheroes","id":353213,"title":"Unexpected Divine Superheroes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-28T16:08:57-08:00","id":353213,"title":"Unexpected Divine Superheroes","content":"This isn\u2019t about Scion, but it is about mythic gods in a modern world, so I hope nobody minds. Besides, this forum has the greatest concentration I know of erudition about mythology and (I hope) willingness to creatively misinterpret those myths.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m building a new superhero setting for my gaming group. Mythological gods becoming superheroes and supervillains has been a standard part of superhero settings at least since Marvel coopted Thor, so I shall include at least a few such heroes. But I want to look beyond the obvious warrior gods and heroes such as Thor, Hercules, Horus, Yi the Archer, etc. Such characters shall appear as NPCs but I don\u2019t want to be limited by them. I want a few divine/mythic heroes my players won't expect.<br /> <br /> Example: I\u2019m going to have Anubis appear as a fairly well-known NPC hero. Anubis? Why Anubis? Well, he has a connection with justice through his participation in the Weighing of the Heart ceremony. He\u2019s a protector of tombs, tomb-goods and the dead, which could give him an interest in the multi-billion-dollar criminal trade in stolen antiquities, as well as people who have died without receiving proper funeral rites \u2013 such as victims of murder and massacre. Anubis solves the average murder as easily as Thor defeats the average mugger: the Jackal God just calls up the victim\u2019s ghost and asks who did it\u2026 which means building stories around unusual murders. Anubis the Psychopomp also guarded the passages between the worlds of the living and the dead, suggesting stories about ghostly and demonic incursions, or battles with vampires and other undead villains. Between bizarre murders, museum robberies, military and supervillain massacres, and undead or otherworldly villains, I think Anubis supplies plenty of hooks for appearances as an NPC guest hero.<br /> <br /> Even for the standard warrior/hero gods, I hope to add a twist. Like, myths about the Mesopotamian hero-god Ninurta mostly deal with him battling demons and monsters, but he also has the divine title of Inspector of Fields and Canals. He\u2019ll be my campaign\u2019s analog to Thor, a big lummox who bashes enemies with his magical mace Expeller. (What does it expel? Consciousness, mostly.) But he\u2019s also active with NGOs that dig wells, build water systems and improve crops and farming practices. Sounds harmless, right? Not to a corrupt Third World government that doesn\u2019t want village folk developing any sort of organization independent of the State. So Ninurta has some rather worldly enemies, too.<br /> <br /> (I'm toying with Daedalus as a clockpunk gadgeteer, too, but probably not a hero. In the myths, He was kind of a bastard.)<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the sort of thing I\u2019m looking for. Divine heroes who are heroic in ways you don\u2019t immediately expect. Any suggestions?<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T17:05:53-08:00","id":353270,"title":"","content":"A semi-regular art idea prompt at Warren Ellis and Si Spurrier's Whitechapel, &quot;Remake/Remodel&quot;, included gods as well as public domain superheroes and the like. I missed the one for <a href=\"http://freakangels.com/whitechapel/comments.php?DiscussionID=7026&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">Glycon</a> the Roman snake god / hand puppet, but was in on the one to make a Marvel Thor style hero out of Egyptian lion, war and beer goddess <a href=\"http://freakangels.com/whitechapel/comments.php?DiscussionID=10127&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">Sekhmet</a>. There are several that mix the obvious heroic potential with the weird sidelines, like Ninurta's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T19:42:54-08:00","id":353369,"title":"","content":"There's certainly plenty to choose from. I think you want to rule out the obvious since by those deities' endeavors most become the rulers of their respective pantheons.<br /> That's one of the things I kinda liked about Siembeda's Rifts is that he seemed to favor Thoth as a big gun. (generally speaking)<br /> <br /> Hmm...looking for a twist...but divine heroes eh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T22:47:07-08:00","id":353526,"title":"","content":"Maybe a hunting god or goddess giving a more-powerful-than-usual spin on the traditional bow-and-arrow heroes? Say, Artemis using various kinds of magic arrows instead of technological gadget arrows?<br /> <br /> Ishtar or whatever was the name of that Mesopotamian goddess of Love and War with the bad temper, fulfilling a role of a particularly irritable Wonder Woman?<br /> <br /> If you want really unexpected, find a way to get Hathor into super-heroing. A motherly heroine with a cow head and cosmic or starlight-based powers ^_^ (well, among her powers, since she was a massively important goddess with a lot of attributions)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T00:47:28-08:00","id":353555,"title":"","content":"You could have a god who wants to do something about their modern reputation, who's had enough of being seen as the bad guy. Set would make a good choice here. (Then there are his roles as god of the desert and storms, not usually paired together in Western cultures; imagine a divine superhero using sand and storm against you.)<br /> <br /> Or take a page from Marvel's Loki comics (Journey into Mystery, Young Avengers, and Loki: Agent of Asgard, which're quite different from his film portrayal): have a god who uses his wits, cunning and trickery to bring down his enemies (or his pantheon's enemies). Hermes, Anansi and Eshu (hell, most trickster gods) would be good for this take.<br /> <br /> Or Thoth as master of knowledge, law, science and magic, making sure that the world's systems stay in balance, that no force wins a decisive victory. Could be quite Sandman/Lucifer-esque.<br /> <br /> Hm... looking at Nephthys' Wikipedia page, she represents divine assistance and protective guardianship, a companion to the dead who protects them on their journey through the afterlife. She's also a nursing mother to the reigning Pharaoh, serving as their ferocious and dangerous guardian, using her firey breath to incinerate the Pharaoh's enemies. In addition, she's a goddess of beer, preventing hangovers, and a goddess of healing. She'd be an interesting superheroine, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T05:14:18-08:00","id":353603,"title":"","content":"I would consider staying away from deities that have already been done in the comic books as they would always draw a person back to those comic books.<br /> <br /> I recall this image and grew very curious about the character:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.comicartcommunity.com/gallery/data/media/601/WARGOD_Pg00.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T06:34:23-08:00","id":353663,"title":"","content":"If you want an amazing duo of superheroes, I can't think of a better pair than the Maya Hero Twins. Hunahpu and Xbalanque are two kickass, blowgunning, forest growing, monster bamboozling, death conquering guys who'd make great superheroes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T09:45:40-08:00","id":353800,"title":"","content":"Riffing off Griff and the OP desire for non-standard potential divine heroes (though weird to modern North American sensibilities in many ways, the Hero Twins are classic heroes), how about their older brothers the monkey gods Hun-Chowen and Hun-Batz? <br /> <br /> They are cast as antagonists of the Twins in the Popul Vuh (and get turned into howler monkeys for it) but they are definitely revered divine figures, patrons of scholarship and artistic pursuits. Howler monkeys can be either cute o rvery intimidating and dangerous, depending on the context. Also, they do have behavior issues. Heroes that can be crass and condescending, physically intimidating and erudite. Potentially all at the same time....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T13:28:06-08:00","id":354036,"title":"","content":"I know the Greek gods better than any others, so I'll stick with those.<br /> <br /> Venus actually had an obscure comic book series for a while. Mostly mystery/horror stories.<br /> <br /> With his prophecy/healing powers, Apollo could make a very interesting Wandering Hero in the style of Kung Fu &amp; other such series. If you don't like him for it, Hermes would do just as well.<br /> <br /> I once did a superhero setting of my own where I took Princess Diana (Wonder Woman) as the current identity for Artemis, so she was more like one of the archer/weapon expert heroes, but with magic instead of tech.<br /> <br /> Athena could really rock as a supernatural investigator. Harry Dresden, but without the necessary learning curve of 15 books, plus Xena. Dionysus could be her Thomas Raith! Drunken party boy who's WAY smarter than he seems.<br /> <br /> If Daedalus is too much of a punk, Hephaestus would fill his spot. I'd read a comic book about a guy who's gadgets and preparedness outstrips Batman and Iron Man combined. Lesser known story, Aphrodite was cheating on him, but it couldn't prove it or catch who it was, so he put an invisible net over his bed to catch them. Not only does this start to show his &quot;crazy prepared&quot; potential, there's also this - he didn't just throw a spell over the net and say &quot;invisible&quot;. He made the chain-link so small and fine as to make it nearly impossible to see, and it was unbreakable. Add to that his Vulcan aspects from the Romans as a god of destruction and fire, and he can be a formidable opponent for anyone.<br /> <br /> &quot;Who knows what evil lurks in the hearts of men..................Erebus knows!&quot;<br /> <br /> Heracles, Perseus, Orpheus and Achilles gets all the press. Jason, Theseus, Bellerophon, Castor &amp; Pollux, and Odysseus don't get NEARLY enough credit for how badass they all are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T17:11:12-08:00","id":355252,"title":"","content":"Thoth might be too high-end for a divine sorcerer hero. I'll probably want to keep him in reserve back in Terra Mythica as someone heroes try to consult -- but it isn't easy. Instead, I'm leaning toward Vainamoinen, from Finnish mythology. Not only is he a great magician and adventuring hero, he's old (though still hale -- the standard description in the Kalevala is &quot;Vainamoinen, old and steadfast&quot;). A senior citizen superhero gives me my twist.<br /> <br /> Years back I'd considered Set as a mercenary semi-hero, though mostly de-powered so he was &quot;just&quot; an immortal soldier badass with several millennia of experience. The Sandman angle is very tempting. I still might use Horus as the &quot;standard&quot; divine hero from the Egyptian pantheon, though. He made the difficult journey from Terra Mythica to the mortal world because it was the only way he could get away from his mother Isis. &quot;Do you know what it's like to be 6,000 years old and still be treated as the baby of the family? To have your mother trying to solve all your problems for you? And let me tell you, her idea of help can be pretty dire.&quot;<br /> <br /> More later. Thank you all for the suggestions!<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T19:32:24-08:00","id":355334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/353213-unexpected-divine-superheroes?p=355252#post355252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoth might be too high-end for a divine sorcerer hero. I'll probably want to keep him in reserve back in Terra Mythica as someone heroes try to consult -- but it isn't easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Thoth, you could have him as the Doctor Strange equivalent. Someone who's totally willing to give advice and consultation and would love to help, but is currently too busy telling the latest tentacled abomination from beyond exactly where they can stuff it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T19:41:04-08:00","id":356177,"title":"","content":"If you want to go for ultimate ridiculousness I can recommend Urcuchillay, the Incan God of Llamas. Because a rainbow colored star llama is a fantastic thing to throw at people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T23:46:19-08:00","id":356340,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always been partial to the idea of Iris, greek goddess of the Rainbow and messenger of the gods, being sent into the modern world on a mission from the gods and getting caught up in current affairs on Earth \u2014 say, Titans have broken out of Tartarus and she\u2019s supposed to find the hero who will drive them back; but something happens with the chosen hero and Iris is the only one in a position to do anything about the breakout. In particular, I\u2019d model it more after espionage shows like Alias or Burn Notice, with Iris\u2019 major strength being how clever she is. In fact, I like the notion that she learns early on that there\u2019s a traitor somewhere in Olympus, and she has to go to ground on Earth while she figures out who it is and gathers the necessary evidence to allow Hera to do something about it. (And if the traitor turns out to be Hermes\u2026 well, she\u2019d have her work cut out for her.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I can hardly wait for Scion and Trinity Continuum: Aberrant to be out; this thread is exactly the sort of thing I\u2019d like to do with said games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-01-2015, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:05:40-08:00","id":356421,"title":"","content":"For inspiration, Wonder Woman became the Greek Goddess of Truth in the original continuity. Thor, of the Marvel universe is also a good candidate, though the name &quot;Thor&quot; seems to be more of a title than an actual name from recent developments. Marvel also tried to make Isis a Divine Superheroine and they have an ongoing series with Hercules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T17:10:22-08:00","id":357901,"title":"","content":"I will definitely look for information about Urcuchillay. Thanks, Griff!<br /> <br /> Iris intrigues me, too. I mean, there's no shortage of potential superheroes in the Greek pantheon. Apollo and Artemis would make a great brother and sister team of supernatural archers, as suggested; with comedy potential for Apollo's womanizing contrasted with Artemis' vow of virginity. Or Athena not only being badass in combat, but an incredible tactician and just plain Smarter Than You at just about everything. Little Miss Overachiever, that's Athena. But Iris is interesting for being one of the less-known, second-tier mythic figures with one big power that's not obviously combat-oriented: She can go anywhere, almost instantly. And if she can carry other people along...<br /> <br /> So, Iris is a mainstay of the Heroes Without Borders NGO super-team. Many regions have the problem of no home-grown superheroes. That makes them targets for supervillains who are smart enough to figure out that trying to rob a bank in New York City is really stupid. When villains start robbing banks in Togo or trying to conquer Sikkim, the government calls Heroes Without Borders, and Iris speeds a team to the spot. And while she may not be that combat-oriented by divine standards she's still a god and no pushover.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T18:50:18-08:00","id":357946,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for some lesser-known gods to use, try some African theologies. Most people know Anansi, but less know Bondye, Nyame, Agwu or Ogun, for example.<br /> <br /> Or Maori: Punga makes a good villain.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to go <i>really</i> obscure, Shinto often includes ancestor worship, and while this is unlikely to make them <i>big</i> gods, having a family revere you for centuries does a spirit good. Particularly if you go for some of the lesser-known Japanese emperors: they'd have some decent backing behind them, Legend-wise (don't know how much of Scion you'd be using, but you get my point).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:36:39-08:00","id":357996,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, like many aspects of pre-Columbian South American religions, much information about Urcuhillay is lost. Our knowledge of him comes primarily from a Jesuit priest and naturalist named Jose de Acosta, who in his book &quot;Natural and Moral History of the Indies&quot;, wrote the following....<br /> <br /> &quot;They attributed different functions to different stars, just as the shepherds adored and sacrificed to a star that they call Urcuchillay, which they say is a ram of many colors that is skilled in the preservation of their flocks and is apparently the one the astronomers call Lyra. And the same Indians adore the two other stars near it, which they call Catuchillay and Urcuchillay, which they fancy to be a ewe with a lamb&quot;<br /> <br /> (note, he says ram/ewe/lamb here, but the rest of the book make it clear that sheep is the term he's using to describe llamas. He similarly calls jaguars &quot;tigers&quot; and pumas &quot;lions&quot;. Also that Urcuchillay is simultaneously male and female, what the hell)<br /> <br /> So... yeah, that's what we know about him, or possibly her, in a nutshell. <br /> <br /> I mainly think he could work in a superhero setting as an oddball hero, but with the possibility of having a tremendous amount of power over entirely circumstantial situations. You could expand the protection of llama herds to protection of all domestic animals, or all animals in general. Or you could have it that a fight between heroes and villains lands in an alpaca farm and thus Urcuchillay warps down from the sky and kicks everyone's ass. <br /> <br /> This also applies to any Scion game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T08:31:31-08:00","id":358338,"title":"","content":"Do you have a nutshell about what the people's involved thought about llamas overall? Did they have specific mythological or other attributions (like we give to lions, elephants, etc.)?<br /> <br /> A South American shining rainbow star transgender superhero/ine sounds pretty boss to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T08:36:24-08:00","id":358340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/353213-unexpected-divine-superheroes?p=357901#post357901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> <br /> So, Iris is a mainstay of the Heroes Without Borders NGO super-team. Many regions have the problem of no home-grown superheroes. That makes them targets for supervillains who are smart enough to figure out that trying to rob a bank in New York City is really stupid. When villains start robbing banks in Togo or trying to conquer Sikkim, the government calls Heroes Without Borders, and Iris speeds a team to the spot. And while she may not be that combat-oriented by divine standards she's still a god and no pushover.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>Does she use rainbows to move people around since those were one of her primary attributes? How do we know Hera has sent Iris on a mission? There's a rainbow in the sky...<br /> <br /> I know rainbows have been mostly bogarted over to the Norse (not to minimize Bifrost, but Iris doesn't have a movie franchise and millions of $$$ in F/X to back her up), but it would seem like an amazing tactical advantage to a superhero group to have a movement specialist. And any Norse folks would be super-comfortable with the transport method as well.<br /> <br /> Also, the possible relation to Uruchillay as another rainbow-aspected deity-type....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T12:32:52-08:00","id":359423,"title":"","content":"Staying away from the gods that were done is good. But if they're from obscure sources that a more general audience (an audience that knows fantasy and myth of course) that will have them think off-handedly it's made up from scratch, then I think the point of this thread is lost.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself ('natch) I'm familiar with Iris. &quot;Urcuchillay?&quot; Is that Kal-El's sister? (It kinda loses something if I have to dig for more info, especially knowing that it's a deity that was once worshipped somewhere on the planet. Or if currently worshipped...well, that just drives the point further.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:02:58-08:00","id":359518,"title":"","content":"Who is Ninurta again? Is he some kind of philosopher? Rap star? <br /> <br /> Oh wait, minor god/hero in relatively obscure myths in not very well known mythology. <br /> <br /> Unfamiliar deities and unfamiliar mythologies were specifically referenced and requested as sources in the original post.<br /> <br /> So.... <br /> <br /> Urcuchillay RULES! If it weren't going to turn out so very &quot;My Little Pony&quot;, I'd definitely buy the t-shirt.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T16:26:33-08:00","id":359648,"title":"","content":"I know my players. They would be tickled by Urcuchillay precisely *because* they've never heard of him/her. But would enjoy learning.<br /> <br /> Documentation is of course an issue once you move beyond the &quot;standard&quot; mythologies such as Greek, Norse, Egyptian. It doesn't help that supposed &quot;standard&quot; reference works are often sparse in information, woefully out of date, and written by people who weren't really experts in their subject.<br /> <br /> Griff's scenario reminds me of the Wheatfield Avenger, an NPC hero from a game some friends of mine were in years ago. He was the great hero of Eastern Washington. Nigh omnipotent... but only if he was in a wheat field. How much crime happens in wheat fields?<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","user":"DShomshak","date":". 01-04-2015, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:55:30-08:00","id":359808,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* I forgot that you were creating a setting for your players.<br /> <br /> I thought you were trying to market something.<br /> <br /> ...don't mind me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:46:36-08:00","id":360203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/353213-unexpected-divine-superheroes?p=358338#post358338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a nutshell about what the people's involved thought about llamas overall? Did they have specific mythological or other attributions (like we give to lions, elephants, etc.)?<br /> <br /> A South American shining rainbow star transgender superhero/ine sounds pretty boss to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I've been looking for references to how llamas were perceived by Andean peoples, and most of what I found refers to llama sacrifices. Llamas were incredibly important, as food, as a source of wool, as a provider of fertilizer, and, in the later history of the Inca empire, as a pack animal. Llamas of different colors were offered in different ways to different deities. White llamas were sacrificed to Inti the sun god, black ones to Illapa the thunder god, spotted ones to Pachamama the earth goddess, etc. <br /> <br /> The best thing I could find about attributes that Andeans gave to llamas was their hardiness and their sure-footed nature. Otherwise they were seen as gifts from the gods, and thus a superlative gift to the gods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T08:52:44-08:00","id":360232,"title":"","content":"Seems kinda like mistaken re-gifting.... <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, these llamas are cool! Maybe the gods would like some?&quot; &lt;SLICE&gt; &quot;Errr..... Didn't they give us the llamas in the first place? Oh well, too late...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:05:50-08:00","id":361351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/353213-unexpected-divine-superheroes?p=358338#post358338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a nutshell about what the people's involved thought about llamas overall? Did they have specific mythological or other attributions (like we give to lions, elephants, etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading... reading... llamas... LOLWUT?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Okay, llama and superhero is cool. Freakazoid or Animaniacs vibe. I would want to see Janus. Boundaries, doorways, beginning and ends, Moving to new countries and keeping up with modern times would seem his thing. In Nomine uses him as 'he's an angel and a demon! at the same time!&quot; <br /> Cthulhu as a superhero, his tentaclly goodness that worships the flying spaghetti monster. <br /> Bacchus and the maenads &quot;by the power of drunken madness I command you to stop! Or I will turn you into a dolphin, or maybe a leopard&quot;. <br /> And I forget, has Koschei the Deathless been mentioned in Scion yet? A hero or villain who can be captured but not killed, and oh yeah he lost his heart 50 years ago.<br /> <br /> And of course, reread American Gods for inspiration.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:25:27-08:00","id":361702,"title":"","content":"Koschei the Deathless is bespoke as the King of Vampires. Ah, Koschei. I remember him fondly from that class on Russian folklore I took so long ago.<br /> <br /> Well, he's the king of one kind of vampires, brought into undeath by the door he opened so long ago. There are other kinds of vampires, too.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}